{#- A structured character render (FR-TURN-1, docs/02 §5's Generation row; #150).

The ``system`` block holds, in order: the story rating's prompt guidance (always first,
FR-RATE-4), the custom instructions, a scenario story's scenario text (#122), the rendering
character's definition, its deflection style and, under per-character partitions, its own true
age ("You are 34.", #170), then ``## What you believe`` (its own belief state, FR-TURN-8; #170's
``core.epistemic.context``: every knowledge section below comes from its ``CharacterContext``),
``## Your private memories`` (its own ``think`` memories, #172),
the pinned memories (#60's text pins), the rolling summary when the profile keeps one, then ``## Scene`` (the place and
who is present, #137), ``## What you remember`` (its working memory, FR-MEM-5), ``## Just now``
(#174: a ``sequential`` turn's earlier primaries' verified beats as it perceived them), ``## Retrieved``
(#141's assembled context) and ``## Canon`` (the facts retrieval found that it may know), then
``## Others present`` (#176: the reactive characters whose reactions it may narrate), then
``## The player asks of you`` (#180, FR-RESP-11: under ``own_character``, what the player's input
described this character doing, as requests to comply with or refuse), then ``## Tracked values``
(#187: the player-visible States it may change and the effect syntax, never a value), then
``## How to change your mind`` (the step contract and the ``think`` cite instruction, when the
character keeps its own beliefs; #168, ``steps_contract.j2``), the beat contract, the requested length as a target in words (#464) and, on a guardrail
regeneration, one constraint line per violated output
policy (#68). The director's notes never appear here (FR-SCN-11: the narrator's alone). The
``user`` block is the player input as the character perceived it (#572: the words it perceived,
an envelope such as "Wren whispers something to Marcus" as its line), the final ``user`` message. The beats come back as the
call's ``response_schema`` (#53). -#}
